WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.110
Set a pendulum swinging.

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.340
One swing takes about 1.4 seconds.

3
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.140
Timing it looks easy: start the stopwatch,

4
00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.920
stop it, done.

5
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.750
Yet physicists let it swing
20 times, time the lot,

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.500
then divide by 20.

7
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:19.480
Twenty times the waiting,
for the same single number.

8
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.360
Why time 20 swings of a
pendulum instead of just one?

9
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.930
In this mission, you'll
plan an experiment:

10
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.800
what you change, what you measure,
and what you keep the same.

11
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:34.040
Then you'll evaluate results: find
the largest source of uncertainty,

12
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.520
and propose a specific fix.

13
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain why timing
20 swings beats timing just one.
